-5\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Sort menu exposes all 4 configured fields plus \\\"Clear sort\\\". Cards sorted by Priority ASC (1,1,2,2,3,4,9) then DESC (9,4,3,2,2,1,1). Table independently sorted by Task Name ASC. Switching Table→Cards kept Cards at Priority DESC; switching Cards→Table kept Table at Task Name ASC. Sort states are per-view and independent.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Field-specific filtering is not implemented — no filter UI exists\", \"actual\": \"The app provides no way to define field-specific filter criteria. The complete set of controls is: Fields, quick-search box (\\\"Search entries...\\\"), Sort (field list + Clear sort), Table/Cards toggle, Add Entry, and per-row edit/delete/drag buttons. The only <input> on the page is the search box; there are no filter controls in the toolbar, in column headers (clicking a header only sorts), or in the Fields dialog. Therefore filter criteria cannot be defined, matching entries cannot be isolated, and there are no filters to clear.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"With sort cleared in both views (footer shows \\\"Drag entries to reorder\\\"), rows/cards expose dnd-kit sortable drag handles. Table: moved \\\"Design new landing page\\\" from position 1 to 3 → [Review, Update, Design, Prepare, Team, Zebra, (blank)]. Cards: independently moved \\\"Design new landing page\\\" from 1 to 2 → [Review, Design, Update, Prepare, Team, Zebra, (blank)]. Switching back to Table showed [Review, Update, Design, ...] — each view kept its own manual order.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Data import is not implemented — no import mechanism exists\", \"actual\": \"Field schema definition works (Configure Fields dialog), but there is no way to import data. The full button set is Fields, Sort, Table, Cards, Add Entry, and column-header sort buttons; there are zero input[type=file] elements and zero textareas anywhere in the document (main page and Fields dialog both checked). The Fields dialog only displays the advisory text \\\"Configure fields before importing data.\\\" with no accompanying import control, file picker, paste area, or CSV/JSON option. Consequently type-mismatch rejection on import cannot occur and could not be exercised.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Priority is input[type=number]; typing \\\"a\\\",\\\"b\\\" produced value \\\"\\\" (chars discarded, no bad input saved). Valid values 7 and 42.5 were accepted and saved, displaying as \\\"7\\\" and \\\"42.5\\\" in the table.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Due Date is input[type=date]. Programmatically setting \\\"2026-02-31\\\" (invalid calendar date) left value \\\"\\\" — it could not be entered or saved. Valid dates 2026-02-28 and 2026-06-01 were accepted and rendered as \\\"Feb 28, 2026\\\" and \\\"Jun 1, 2026\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Before sort: 7 entries. After Priority ASC (1,1,2,2,3,4,9) and Priority DESC (9,4,3,2,2,1,1) the count stayed \\\"7 entries\\\" and every field value was intact, e.g. Zebra Deployment Plan|P=9|Feb 28, 2026|Yes and Team sync meeting notes|P=2|Jan 14, 2026|Yes. Only ordering changed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Cannot verify filter inclusion/clearing because filtering does not exist\", \"actual\": \"No filtering capability is present in the app (no filter controls in toolbar, column headers, or Fields dialog; the only input is the quick-search box). With no active criteria to satisfy and no filters to clear, this constraint cannot be met.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Empty value has no clear representation and is rendered inconsistently between views and across field types\", \"actual\": \"An entry saved with an empty Task Name (text) renders with no representation at all: in table view the Task Name cell innerHTML is \\\"\\\" (completely blank, no placeholder), and in card view the card has no h3 heading element at all (last card innerText = \\\"PRIORITY\\\\n4\\\\nDUE DATE\\\\nJun 1, 2026\\\\nCOMPLETED\\\\nNo\\\"), so the entry appears unlabeled/anonymous. By contrast an empty Number field (the added \\\"Score\\\" column) did render a clear \\\"—\\\" placeholder in table view, so empty handling is inconsistent across field types too.\", \"evidence\": \"Non-empty values are otherwise consistent between the two views (all 7 entries, matching values).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Field config dialog labels each type explicitly (Text, Number, Date, Checkbox) with dropdown options. Entry form renders input[type=text] for Task Name, input[type=number] for Priority/Score, input[type=date] for Due Date, and a role=checkbox toggle for Completed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Entry form: role=checkbox toggle with data-state=\\\"checked\\\"/aria-checked=\\\"true\\\" and adjacent label switching \\\"No\\\"→\\\"Yes\\\". Table view: green lucide-check icon (text-success) for true vs muted lucide-x icon for false. Card view: explicit \\\"Yes\\\"/\\\"No\\\" text with icon. States are distinguishable in all three places.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Quick search matches internal raw values instead of the displayed formatted dates and checkbox states\", \"actual\": \"Dates: the table displays \\\"Feb 28, 2026\\\" for Zebra Deployment Plan, but searching \\\"Feb 28, 2026\\\" returns \\\"0 entries matching\\\" and \\\"Feb\\\" returns \\\"0 entries matching\\\"; searching the raw ISO value \\\"2026-02-28\\\" returns 1 entry. Checkboxes: several entries display \\\"Yes\\\" (Completed), yet searching \\\"Yes\\\" returns \\\"0 entries matching\\\". Searching \\\"No\\\" returned only \\\"Team sync meeting notes\\\" — a substring match on the text \\\"notes\\\", not the four entries whose Completed displays \\\"No\\\". So formatted dates and checkbox states shown to users are not searchable.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Query \\\"MARKETING\\\" (uppercase) matched lowercase \\\"Review marketing materials\\\" — 1 row, label \\\"1 entry matching \\\\\\\"MARKETING\\\\\\\"\\\". Lowercase \\\"marketing\\\" gave the same result. Clearing the box restored all 7 rows with label \\\"7 entries\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Selecting \\\"Priority\\\" from the Sort menu immediately reordered cards to 1,1,2,2,3,4,9. The Sort button label changed from \\\"Sort\\\" to \\\"Priority\\\" with a lucide-arrow-up icon (ascending); re-selecting toggled to lucide-arrow-down with order 9,4,3,2,2,1,1. Menu also marks the active field and offers \\\"Clear sort\\\". App remained fully interactive.\"}]}"
