  "payload": {
    "role": "assistant",
    "type": "assistant_message",
    "content": "All 18 checklist items have been tested and recorded — coverage is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**12 PASS / 6 FAIL**\n\n**Working well:** field configuration with all four types, entry creation with type-appropriate controls, number/date input validation, view switching, per-view independent sorting (including direction toggle and active-field indication), per-view independent manual drag reordering, checkbox state rendering, and case-insensitive quick search with live result counts.\n\n**Six failures, three of them missing features:**\n\n- **FT-6 / CS-12 — Filtering does not exist.** There is no filter UI anywhere: not in the toolbar, not in column headers (which only sort), not in the Fields dialog. The only input on the page is the search box. A core requirement from the brief is entirely absent.\n- **FT-19 — Import does not exist.** The Fields dialog displays the advisory \"Configure fields before importing data,\" but there is no import control, file picker, or paste area anywhere (zero `input[type=file]`, zero `textarea` in the document). The type-mismatch rejection behavior therefore cannot occur.\n- **FT-1 — No persistence.** Entries and field definitions are held in memory only; `localStorage` is empty. A created entry and an added field both vanished on reload, reverting to the 5 seed entries. The \"appears immediately\" half works; the \"remains after reload\" half does not.\n- **CS-20 — Search matches raw values, not displayed ones.** `\"Feb 28, 2026\"` (the text actually shown) returns 0 results while the raw `\"2026-02-28\"` returns 1. Likewise `\"Yes\"` returns 0 despite entries visibly displaying \"Yes\". Note that searching `\"No\"` returns a misleading single hit — that is a substring match on \"notes\", not a checkbox match.\n- **CS-13 — Empty values render as nothing, inconsistently.** An empty text value produces a completely blank table cell and a card with no heading element at all, leaving the entry visually anonymous. An empty number field, by contrast, correctly renders a \"—\" placeholder — so the handling is inconsistent across field types as well as unclear to users.\n\nOne note on scope: the checklist premise that \"sort states are saved automatically\" could not be validated as durable, since the FT-1 persistence failure means no state survives a reload; sort independence was verified only within a session."
  }
}
